    "sam.acf.shockdef": "ACF: definite dehydration (history of fluid loss and a recent change in the eyes) AND all of — semi-conscious or unconscious, rapid weak pulse, cold hands and feet, poor capillary refill in the nail beds.",
    "sam.acf.diag.1": "Do not use the skin pinch or sunken eyes to diagnose dehydration in marasmus — both are usually present without dehydration.",
    "sam.acf.diag.2": "Diagnose from the history: definite recent watery diarrhoea; the carer says the eyes became sunken since the diarrhoea began; no visible full superficial veins; and no oedema. Make a provisional diagnosis and confirm it by the response to treatment.",
    "sam.acf.diag.3": "Before starting: weigh the child (naked), mark the liver edge on the skin, and record breathing rate (and, if possible, pulse, capillary refill and heart sounds).",
    "sam.acf.oedema.h": "Oedema present — ACF",
    "sam.acf.oedema": "Children with oedema have excess body water and sodium: they cannot be 'dehydrated', although they are often hypovolaemic. Do not treat the hypotension of kwashiorkor with ReSoMal or IV fluid. If there is definite watery diarrhoea and the child is deteriorating, replace losses with 30 mL ReSoMal per watery stool.",
    "sam.acf.noloss.h": "No weight loss — ACF",
