    "sam.acf.shock.4": "If there is no improvement although the weight has increased: assume toxic, septic or cardiogenic shock or liver failure — stop rehydration and look for other causes.",
    "sam.acf.a.h": "No dehydration (ACF)",
    "sam.acf.a.1": "No 'preventive' ReSoMal. For children 6–24 months, 30 mL ReSoMal may be given per watery stool to replace losses — do not give 50–100 mL per stool.",
