    "sam.acf.target.est": "Newly admitted: estimate the deficit conservatively — usually 1–3% of body weight, at most 5%. Upper limit {tw} kg (current weight + 5%); do not exceed it in a conscious child.",
    "sam.acf.oral.1": "ReSoMal orally or by NG tube at {r10} mL/h (10 mL/kg/h) for the first 2 h (about 2% of body weight). Weigh every hour; check liver size, breathing rate, capillary refill and pulse.",
    "sam.acf.oral.2": "At 2 h: weight still falling → increase by 10 mL/kg/h (to {r20} mL/h); no weight gain → increase by 5 mL/kg/h (to {r15} mL/h); reassess in 1 h.",
    "sam.acf.oral.3": "Weight gain with deterioration, or no clinical improvement: the diagnosis of dehydration was probably wrong — stop and start F-75. Improving but still dehydrated: continue cautiously to the target weight (ReSoMal alone or alternating with F-75).",
